# Onboard sensors

The accelerometer, gyroscope, magnetometer and proximity sensor run on
the phone's sensor DSP. `ExQcomSmgr` keeps the latest reading of each.

## Read every sensor once

```elixir
ExQcomSmgr.read_all()
```

Units: accelerometer in m/s², gyroscope in rad/s, magnetometer in gauss.
`{:error, :no_data}` means that sensor hasn't reported yet.

## One sensor

```elixir
ExQcomSmgr.read(:accel)
```

## Live view

Tilt the phone while this runs for ten seconds.

```elixir
frame = Kino.Frame.new() |> Kino.render()

for _ <- 1..50 do
  text =
    case ExQcomSmgr.read(:accel) do
      {:ok, %{x: x, y: y, z: z}} ->
        "x: #{Float.round(x, 2)}   y: #{Float.round(y, 2)}   z: #{Float.round(z, 2)}  m/s²"

      other ->
        inspect(other)
    end

  Kino.Frame.render(frame, Kino.Markdown.new("`#{text}`"))
  Process.sleep(200)
end

:done
```

## Proximity

Cover the top of the phone with your hand and read again.

```elixir
ExQcomSmgr.read(:prox)
```
